# Typed Supabase Mutations

ALWAYS type `update`, `insert`, and `upsert` calls with the corresponding `Database` type from `@/app/api/database.types`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
supabase.from('projects').update({ name: 'foo' })
supabase.from('projects').insert({ name: 'foo' })

// ✅ GOOD
import { Database } from '@/app/api/database.types'

supabase.from('projects').update<Database['public']['Tables']['projects']['Update']>({ name: 'foo' })
supabase.from('projects').insert<Database['public']['Tables']['projects']['Insert']>({ name: 'foo' })
```
